Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the overlay's ImGui frame time from the steady clock, not raylib's GetFrameTime (TODO 404)

rlImGuiBegin() hands ImGui raylib's GetFrameTime(), which raylib sets only in EndDrawing(). With the DXGI swap chain
(the default on Windows, ps2_host_present.cpp) the pictures are presented without EndDrawing, and since patch 0196 not
one picture of a session goes through it: the value stays 0 and rlImGui turned that into 0.001 s a frame. ImGui's clock
then ran at 6% of real time at 60 pictures a second (24% at 240): held arrow keys barely repeated in the F1 menu, hover
and tooltip delays dragged on, two separate clicks could count as a double-click, scrolling crawled.

The rlImGui host now measures the time between two overlay frames on the steady clock and begins the frame with
rlImGuiBeginDelta(dt), clamped to 1/1000 to 1/10 s (the first frame, and the first after the overlay was closed, count as
1/60 or 1/10). Nothing about the pictures' pacing changes. The SDL3 platform's host is not this one (its ImGui backend
takes its own time) and is untouched.
---
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_overlay.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_overlay.cpp
@@ -3,17 +3,34 @@
 
 #include "rlImGui.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <chrono>
+
 namespace ps2_overlay
 {
     namespace
     {
+        // (TODO 404) The time since the overlay's last frame, on the steady clock: raylib's GetFrameTime() is set only
+        // in EndDrawing(), which the DXGI present path never calls (0 all session). Clamped to [1/1000, 1/10] s; the first
+        // frame counts as 1/60.
+        float frameSeconds()
+        {
+            using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+            static Clock::time_point last{};
+            const Clock::time_point now = Clock::now();
+            const bool first = last == Clock::time_point{};
+            const float dt = first ? 1.0f / 60.0f : std::chrono::duration<float>(now - last).count();
+            last = now;
+            return std::clamp(dt, 0.001f, 0.1f);
+        }
+
         Host rlImGuiHost()
         {
             Host h;
             h.name = "rlImGui";
             h.setup = [](bool darkTheme) { rlImGuiSetup(darkTheme); };
             h.shutdown = [] { rlImGuiShutdown(); };
-            h.begin = [] { rlImGuiBegin(); };
+            h.begin = [] { rlImGuiBeginDelta(frameSeconds()); };
             h.end = [] { rlImGuiEnd(); };
             return h;
         }
